From 6f84db6ec94fa8e50a0d4b204ca586ae9df1b1eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sinai <sinai.rusinek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:30:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Render PAGE TableCell regions, not just TextRegion

The viewer walks TextRegion -> TextLine, so PAGE files whose text lives in
TableCell render as empty: no polygons, no transcription. That is the normal
layout for tabular sources (registers, ledgers, censuses, account books)
exported from Transkribus, where each cell carries its own Coords and
TextEquiv.

This teaches the existing region path to treat TableCell as a region:

- collectRegions() gathers TextRegion and TableCell, matching on localName so
  it works whatever the PAGE namespace prefix is
- ownCoords() reads an element's OWN Coords child rather than the first
  descendant, so a cell's polygon is the cell and not its first line
- cells are drawn from their own Coords, so a cell with geometry but no text
  still renders -- useful while checking segmentation before transcription
- cells are coloured by column index and labelled "Cell r3 c8" from the
  row/col attributes, so a mis-assigned column is visible at a glance
- the inline region/line walking is factored into collectRegions(),
  collectLines(), ownCoords() and parsePoints(), which is what makes the
  TableCell case a few lines rather than a fourth copy of the loop

No behaviour change for prose manuscripts. Verified against the sample data
in this repository: 67 pages, 76 regions, 2258 lines -- region and line
extraction is identical before and after.

Tested additionally on a 98-page Arabic tax register (19 columns, ~35 rows
per page): 667 cell and 412 line polygons on a representative page, no
console errors.
